The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> is compatible with the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-pencil/">Apple Pencil</a>, if you have the right one. <em>MacRumors</em> videographer Dan Barbera tested the &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; with the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; to see if it's a useful tool to pick up.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe title="Apple Pencil on iPhone Duo: Is It Useful?" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/7xpgdj7Rbjk" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe></div><br/>
If you already have an &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; 1, &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; 2, or &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; Pro to use with an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a>, you're going to be disappointed to hear they won't work with the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;. The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; only works with the &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; with USB-C, which is &#36;79 from Apple, but you can get it <a href="https://buy.geni.us/Proxy.ashx?TSID=3088&GR_URL=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.amazon.com%2FApple-MUWA3AM-A-Pencil-USB-C%2Fdp%2FB0CL7J12YK">from Amazon for &#36;69</a>.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; Pro attaches to and pairs with iPads magnetically, but the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; has to be paired with the USB-C &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; using a USB-C cable. &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; support is being added in iOS 27.2, which is available in beta right now.<br/>
<br/>
Once paired, the &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; works with the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; like it works with an &zwnj;iPad&zwnj;. You can write or draw, and there is a setting to turn on palm rejection. You can use the &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; on both the inner and outer displays. The &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; can attach magnetically to the Duo's hinge for storage, but it doesn't charge that way.<br/>
<br/>
Compared with the &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; Pro, the USB-C &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; doesn't have pressure sensitivity, double-tap, or squeeze.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; tip can leave lines on the Duo's display, but the lines wipe away with a polishing cloth. Permanent damage is unlikely, but Apple does have an &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/14/iphone-duo-repair-fees/">cover layer replacement option</a> that's &#36;19 if you have <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/applecare/">AppleCare</a>+ and &#36;49 if you don't.<br/>
<br/>
If you want to take notes or make quick sketches with the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;, the &zwnj;Apple Pencil&zwnj; with USB-C could be worth the cost, but it's not quite as useful as it is on an &zwnj;iPad&zwnj; due to the limited screen size.<div class="linkback">Related Roundup: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a></div><div class="linkback">Tag: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-pencil/">Apple Pencil</a></div><div class="linkback">Buyer's Guide: <a href="https://buyersguide.macrumors.com/#iPhone-Duo">iPhone Duo (Buy Now)</a></div><div class="linkback">Related Forums: <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/forums/iphone.99">iPhone</a>, <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/forums/ipad-accessories.139">iPad Accessories</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/23/iphone-duo-apple-pencil/">Using an Apple Pencil With the iPhone Duo: What to Know</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/using-an-apple-pencil-with-the-iphone-duo-what-to-know.2492537/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>